1
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,055
In the language of flowers,
a black rose means

2
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:12,305
"I will resent you till the day I die."

3
00:00:31,139 --> 00:00:35,722
5 CONTESTANTS LEFT.
4 DAYS AND 3 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME ENDS.

4
00:00:38,097 --> 00:00:42,389
PM 03:00 JST
TOKYO

5
00:00:44,055 --> 00:00:48,972
"I have a gift for my players.
Video conference in one hour."

6
00:00:49,722 --> 00:00:52,180
We have to access this link...

7
00:00:52,847 --> 00:00:54,097
What?!

8
00:00:54,222 --> 00:00:55,264
PM 02:00 SGT
SINGAPORE

9
00:00:56,764 --> 00:00:58,139
One hour?!

10
00:01:00,805 --> 00:01:02,972
It's impossible...

11
00:01:06,597 --> 00:01:08,555
PM 03:00 JST
NAHA

12
00:01:08,764 --> 00:01:11,222
"Participate or be disqualified."

13
00:01:28,014 --> 00:01:30,222
PM 02:00 HKT
HONG KONG

14
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:32,139
A "gift"?

15
00:01:32,639 --> 00:01:33,972
Another message?

16
00:01:34,555 --> 00:01:37,389
How dare they?
Don't they know who I am?

17
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:41,930
What does he want us to do?

18
00:01:44,055 --> 00:01:47,014
They're from that "GAME" thing on TV.

19
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,847
Let's go.

20
00:02:10,264 --> 00:02:11,680
I bought it for tomorrow.

21
00:02:12,017 --> 00:02:14,513
-Tomorrow?
-Did you forget?

22
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:20,639
No way I'd forget. It's our... tenth.

23
00:02:57,173 --> 00:03:00,288
Even so, considering the scale,

24
00:03:00,403 --> 00:03:03,403
a crime syndicate must be behind it.

25
00:03:04,111 --> 00:03:08,496
We've also received some special footage.
Please take a look.

26
00:03:09,111 --> 00:03:13,195
It was recorded moments ago
in Teito TV's newsroom.

27
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:18,403
The man in black is thought to belong
to the criminal organization.

28
00:03:18,528 --> 00:03:20,236
However, the man...

29
00:03:20,361 --> 00:03:22,929
You promised not to use that footage.

30
00:03:22,986 --> 00:03:25,778
Is there anything misleading in it?

31
00:03:25,903 --> 00:03:30,070
It contains the truth.
Reporting it is our job.

32
00:03:30,195 --> 00:03:34,278
People need to know how violent
Toshiro Niide is.

33
00:03:34,445 --> 00:03:37,153
-Niide is...
-Put your feelings aside!

34
00:03:38,903 --> 00:03:44,820
We're seeing a heinous, unprecedented,
global kidnapping case.

35
00:03:44,945 --> 00:03:47,820
And you're stuck in the middle of it.

36
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:52,445
Make the most
of your journalistic good fortune.

37
00:03:59,445 --> 00:04:05,695
The man attacking him appears to be "Wrath,"
a police detective working in Tokyo,

38
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:11,945
while the man in glasses accompanying him
seems to be a doctor from Seoul.

39
00:04:12,570 --> 00:04:15,278
We're global celebrities now.

40
00:04:16,778 --> 00:04:18,653
How did we get here?

41
00:04:22,736 --> 00:04:27,528
The enemy's greater than we thought.

42
00:04:27,653 --> 00:04:31,195
They're enjoying watching us squirm.

43
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:35,861
No matter who they are, Saori...

44
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:41,111
everyone is coming home safe.

45
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:43,903
That's our goal.

46
00:04:52,236 --> 00:04:55,445
2 MINUTES UNTIL THE VIDEO CONFERENCE

47
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:27,070
Tokyo and Seoul, I see.

48
00:05:27,445 --> 00:05:30,861
Perhaps we should introduce ourselves.

49
00:05:31,028 --> 00:05:34,153
Toshiro Niide, Tokyo.
Are you the Hong Kong player?

50
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:39,653
I saw your video.
You shouldn't resort to violence, detective.

51
00:05:48,361 --> 00:05:51,861
Her son Kuranosuke is a software engineer,

52
00:05:51,986 --> 00:05:53,903
fairly famous in IT circles.

53
00:05:55,236 --> 00:05:58,278
Can you trace the host?

54
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:05,028
Please, we all need to work together.

55
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,528
What's so funny?

56
00:06:11,358 --> 00:06:16,358
The criminal arranged this meeting,
fully aware that we will discuss this.

57
00:06:16,483 --> 00:06:20,608
So, it's impossible to chase the host,

58
00:06:21,150 --> 00:06:23,483
even for a skilled software engineer.

59
00:06:24,566 --> 00:06:27,691
So you checked us out
while hiding your own identity.

60
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:30,650
Gotta hand it to you, shyster.

61
00:06:30,983 --> 00:06:33,066
That's a bit rich coming from you.

62
00:06:33,191 --> 00:06:34,316
What?!

63
00:06:35,816 --> 00:06:39,316
Sorry! Oh, I made it!

64
00:06:39,525 --> 00:06:41,358
Your connection isn't very good.

65
00:06:42,066 --> 00:06:44,275
I'm in a tunnel!

66
00:06:46,525 --> 00:06:50,191
You're the Tokyo guy, right?
Thanks for your help.

67
00:06:50,650 --> 00:06:52,275
It's not like I...

68
00:06:52,525 --> 00:06:54,525
Guess what was the clue
for my third checkpoint.

69
00:06:55,191 --> 00:06:57,525
"Climb towards the yellow rain."

70
00:06:57,691 --> 00:07:01,025
So, I've got no choice but to take the call here.
If not, I'd run out of time.

71
00:07:01,525 --> 00:07:02,775
Awful, right?

72
00:07:04,650 --> 00:07:07,566
Hello?

73
00:07:07,858 --> 00:07:09,775
Oh, no! Hello?

74
00:07:10,650 --> 00:07:12,983
Ah, can you hear me now?

75
00:07:15,608 --> 00:07:18,191
Best not to talk about missions here.

76
00:07:19,941 --> 00:07:21,566
Why not?

77
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:27,303
Yes, why not?
"We need to work together," right? Don't we?

78
00:07:29,403 --> 00:07:30,070
Who are you?

79
00:07:30,596 --> 00:07:33,816
He's a lawyer from Hong Kong.
Be careful what you say.

80
00:07:34,383 --> 00:07:35,150
To anyone.

81
00:07:52,983 --> 00:07:54,983
Is someone there? Show your face!

82
00:07:55,108 --> 00:07:58,775
Please, stop this madness
and let Rian go, right now!

83
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:04,025
Please, please let Tony go!
I'll do whatever you want!

84
00:08:05,797 --> 00:08:08,047
I will warn you only once.

85
00:08:08,172 --> 00:08:12,089
Players who disrupt the game
will be instantly disqualified.

86
00:08:15,297 --> 00:08:17,797
I will now distribute your gifts.

87
00:08:23,919 --> 00:08:28,426
What? This is our gift?

88
00:08:30,422 --> 00:08:33,710
One vote each. That's my gift to you.

89
00:08:36,797 --> 00:08:39,210
You may vote to eject a player from the game.

90
00:08:40,630 --> 00:08:45,964
The player with the most votes
will be eliminated.

91
00:08:48,330 --> 00:08:53,396
Naturally, death awaits the loved one
of player who is eliminated.

92
00:08:55,755 --> 00:09:01,005
Now, choose who among the five to eliminate.

93
00:09:45,755 --> 00:09:48,005
KIDNAP GAME

94
00:09:51,589 --> 00:09:57,380
Select the person to be eliminated
from the designated site.

95
00:09:57,505 --> 00:10:00,964
The final vote is in 24 hours.

96
00:10:01,089 --> 00:10:05,297
Until then, you are free to keep revoting.

97
00:10:05,964 --> 00:10:09,380
You're asking us to eliminate someone?

98
00:10:09,656 --> 00:10:14,630
It's only the sixth day!
You said the time limit was ten days!

99
00:10:14,876 --> 00:10:17,005
Why are you doing this to us?!

100
00:10:17,547 --> 00:10:21,255
So that it will be a fitting hell
for your torment.

101
00:10:21,797 --> 00:10:23,922
What if we all vote for ourselves?

102
00:10:24,089 --> 00:10:27,380
Then we'd all have the same number of votes.
What happens then?

103
00:10:27,908 --> 00:10:29,716
No one will be eliminated.

104
00:10:30,486 --> 00:10:34,035
Then to hell with voting!
We just need to not vote.

105
00:10:38,422 --> 00:10:39,672
Kiju?

106
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:43,755
Can you trust everyone here?

107
00:10:45,630 --> 00:10:47,172
Exactly.

108
00:10:47,422 --> 00:10:49,547
How could I trust strangers like you?

109
00:10:53,047 --> 00:10:55,214
We are faced with the prisoner's dilemma.

110
00:10:56,722 --> 00:10:57,576
What's that?

111
00:10:58,350 --> 00:11:02,422
Say there are two prisoners, A and B.

112
00:11:02,589 --> 00:11:06,303
To make them confess,
a prosecutor offers each a plea bargain.

113
00:11:07,373 --> 00:11:09,206
There are three possible outcomes.

114
00:11:09,568 --> 00:11:12,417
Outcome one: both prisoners stay silent.

115
00:11:13,270 --> 00:11:16,380
Their sentences are reduced
from five years to two.

116
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:19,682
Outcome two: one of them confesses.

117
00:11:19,903 --> 00:11:23,636
He's set free,
and the other is given a ten-year sentence.

118
00:11:24,370 --> 00:11:27,089
Outcome three: both of them confess...

119
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:29,316
and both get five years in prison.

120
00:11:30,088 --> 00:11:32,515
So, what should the prisoners do?

121
00:11:38,563 --> 00:11:43,021
I mean, if they both stay silent,
they only get two years... isn't that best?

122
00:11:43,146 --> 00:11:45,730
Yes, but both will confess.

123
00:11:45,855 --> 00:11:49,521
Because humans only care about themselves.

124
00:11:54,316 --> 00:11:56,364
That's how you play into the crook's hands!?

125
00:12:03,688 --> 00:12:06,521
This meeting will end when I exit.

126
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:09,443
We will reconvene in 24 hours.

127
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:11,850
Wait!

128
00:12:13,688 --> 00:12:19,050
What if someone completes their mission
in the next 24 hours?

129
00:12:20,716 --> 00:12:23,750
The game will end,
and there will be no vote.

130
00:12:26,343 --> 00:12:27,336
Understood.

131
00:12:34,188 --> 00:12:37,938
END OF VIDEO CONFERENCE

132
00:13:03,646 --> 00:13:08,490
What is this?
Who am I supposed to vote for?

133
00:13:11,437 --> 00:13:15,923
They're so cocky...
but nobody prevails over my talent, right?

134
00:13:16,755 --> 00:13:20,797
Good point.
The most talented one will surely prevail.

135
00:13:26,813 --> 00:13:29,271
Information! Get me information!

136
00:14:44,436 --> 00:14:47,150
Mission? What mission?

137
00:14:47,175 --> 00:14:48,395
PM 04:26 KST

138
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:52,426
They released a manifesto.
There's no way you don't know.

139
00:14:53,596 --> 00:14:54,656
What do you mean?

140
00:14:55,343 --> 00:14:59,210
For your own sake as well.

141
00:15:07,177 --> 00:15:10,635
RETRIBUTION FOR PROFITEERING

142
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,593
SUBPAR PRODUCTS

143
00:15:12,718 --> 00:15:15,056
DAUGHTER A VICTIM OF PARENTS' GREED

144
00:15:15,466 --> 00:15:17,423
We're victims.
They took our daughter.

145
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,943
Why are they attacking us?

146
00:15:21,677 --> 00:15:26,843
-Hurry up and find her!
-Please leave.

147
00:15:43,468 --> 00:15:45,760
AYUN

148
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:40,718
PREGNANCY AND CHILDBIRTH

149
00:16:48,343 --> 00:16:51,093
WHY MEN MUST SUPPORT THEIR PARTNERS

150
00:16:53,385 --> 00:16:55,260
Just hypothetically...

151
00:16:56,052 --> 00:16:59,427
If we had a baby,
how about the name "Nozomi"?

152
00:18:26,683 --> 00:18:28,996
Sorry I couldn't cook anything.

153
00:18:36,197 --> 00:18:40,530
Your wife loved cooking, right?

154
00:18:42,941 --> 00:18:47,163
Yeah, she was always thinking of my health.

155
00:18:50,941 --> 00:18:52,482
What a wonderful wife.

156
00:18:54,899 --> 00:18:59,232
I caused her nothing but worry.

157
00:19:00,066 --> 00:19:02,149
When I considered quitting...

158
00:19:03,316 --> 00:19:06,857
Swear to me.
That you'll do what's right.

159
00:19:07,857 --> 00:19:11,524
Put your anger aside.
Show me your kindness...

160
00:19:12,566 --> 00:19:16,191
Kindness that shields the weak...

161
00:19:16,816 --> 00:19:23,899
That's the right thing for you to do.

162
00:19:25,441 --> 00:19:27,066
The "right thing."

163
00:19:27,816 --> 00:19:31,399
She comforted me, and supported me.

164
00:19:33,857 --> 00:19:40,357
But I never truly made the effort
to understand her.

165
00:19:42,607 --> 00:19:44,482
She wanted a baby.

166
00:19:48,524 --> 00:19:54,774
But I was abused by my father
when I was a child.

167
00:19:57,816 --> 00:20:00,566
I didn't know if I'd be a good dad.

168
00:20:04,107 --> 00:20:08,232
So I always brushed her comments aside.

169
00:20:10,357 --> 00:20:13,982
Hey, so... Just hypothetically...

170
00:20:14,357 --> 00:20:18,149
If we had a baby,
how about the name "Nozomi"?

171
00:20:19,191 --> 00:20:24,232
-Nozomi?
-Yeah, as in "hope."

172
00:20:24,524 --> 00:20:26,982
It'd work for a boy or a girl.

173
00:20:27,332 --> 00:20:29,903
Yeah, that's not bad.

174
00:20:36,243 --> 00:20:37,107
Yeah...

175
00:20:39,372 --> 00:20:41,831
In the future Saori dreamed of...

176
00:20:44,403 --> 00:20:46,028
we had a child.

177
00:20:49,774 --> 00:20:53,274
But even so, I...

178
00:21:01,732 --> 00:21:03,232
There's still time.

179
00:21:05,941 --> 00:21:10,066
You can still make her dream come true.

180
00:21:11,941 --> 00:21:16,482
That's what you're fighting
so hard for, isn't it?

181
00:21:20,399 --> 00:21:21,357
Yeah.

182
00:21:23,982 --> 00:21:25,316
With you, right?

183
00:21:27,274 --> 00:21:28,566
In my case...

184
00:21:32,357 --> 00:21:33,691
Look at this.

185
00:21:35,857 --> 00:21:38,441
My wife is being slandered.

186
00:21:41,774 --> 00:21:44,149
She's called me several times.

187
00:21:46,941 --> 00:21:48,982
She's also messaged me.

188
00:21:51,147 --> 00:21:54,434
But I can't bear to look...

189
00:21:56,692 --> 00:21:58,983
Whatever it takes, do it!

190
00:22:02,649 --> 00:22:08,482
I don't know... what to do.

191
00:22:12,485 --> 00:22:16,350
I will complete my mission and save Rian,
by any means possible.

192
00:22:20,190 --> 00:22:22,024
That's why you asked that?

193
00:22:22,316 --> 00:22:27,566
What if someone completes their mission
in the next twenty-four hours?

194
00:22:36,118 --> 00:22:37,410
Think, Kiju!

195
00:22:38,405 --> 00:22:40,599
Save her and the rest will die!

196
00:22:40,624 --> 00:22:42,183
If I'm voted out, Rian...

197
00:22:42,208 --> 00:22:44,166
I won't let that happen.

198
00:22:44,770 --> 00:22:48,690
-Is someone else going to take the fall?
-I won't let anyone die.

199
00:22:50,810 --> 00:22:52,774
Only if nobody votes.

200
00:22:53,770 --> 00:22:57,691
But someone will.
And it only takes one.

201
00:23:01,941 --> 00:23:04,107
There's a worse possibility.

202
00:23:05,257 --> 00:23:05,937
What?

203
00:23:06,437 --> 00:23:09,790
The other three...
Are they really just players?

204
00:23:10,883 --> 00:23:11,857
What do you mean?

205
00:23:12,382 --> 00:23:13,923
What if one is the mastermind?

206
00:23:14,590 --> 00:23:17,163
-You're overthinking.
-What about you?

207
00:23:19,424 --> 00:23:23,382
What if you're waiting
for everyone else to die?

208
00:23:24,924 --> 00:23:29,090
You said earlier
that you were going to save Saori.

209
00:23:32,799 --> 00:23:34,674
It's only natural.

210
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:40,090
You want to make her dream come true.

211
00:23:43,424 --> 00:23:48,507
I have Rian's dreams to protect.

212
00:23:50,590 --> 00:23:53,465
I couldn't save her sight.

213
00:23:55,632 --> 00:24:02,965
I have to make amends.
My hands shake and I can't even grip the scalpel.

214
00:24:03,257 --> 00:24:04,590
But even so...

215
00:24:06,715 --> 00:24:08,965
Rian continues to play the cello.

216
00:24:09,090 --> 00:24:11,382
She dreams of being a cellist.

217
00:24:13,382 --> 00:24:14,283
Hope.

218
00:24:16,553 --> 00:24:20,403
She's my hope.

219
00:24:21,743 --> 00:24:22,993
I don't matter.

220
00:24:24,202 --> 00:24:29,343
I have to save Rian.
For her sake, I'll...

221
00:24:29,415 --> 00:24:34,207
Kiju! Don't be hasty.
We'll rescue all the hostages.

222
00:24:36,243 --> 00:24:37,618
Right?

223
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:57,035
Saori!

224
00:25:00,827 --> 00:25:02,410
There's still time.

225
00:25:03,827 --> 00:25:07,368
You can still make her dream come true.

226
00:25:16,577 --> 00:25:21,743
ELIMINATION GAME
10 HOURS UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

227
00:25:21,868 --> 00:25:23,660
AM 06:05 JST

228
00:25:49,285 --> 00:25:51,743
NOTIFICATION

229
00:26:53,839 --> 00:26:56,589
So, what language shall we speak?

230
00:26:58,214 --> 00:27:00,149
Any language is fine for me.

231
00:27:01,714 --> 00:27:03,255
How about Japanese?

232
00:27:04,255 --> 00:27:05,255
Sure.

233
00:27:06,339 --> 00:27:11,672
This is what some call a power spot.
I've had my share of blessings.

234
00:27:12,255 --> 00:27:13,505
Get to the point.

235
00:27:13,964 --> 00:27:15,964
Sorry about yesterday.

236
00:27:16,880 --> 00:27:22,589
I had to hide my intentions
from the mastermind.

237
00:27:23,380 --> 00:27:24,505
What intentions?

238
00:27:26,547 --> 00:27:32,643
Only one can prevail,
but you're working together... Why?

239
00:27:35,386 --> 00:27:36,837
To save everyone.

240
00:27:37,339 --> 00:27:39,839
He agreed to help.

241
00:27:40,254 --> 00:27:41,730
Makes sense.

242
00:27:43,288 --> 00:27:45,872
I also want to save everyone.

243
00:27:48,835 --> 00:27:52,669
Then you'll help us?

244
00:27:53,089 --> 00:27:54,496
Of course I will.

245
00:27:56,047 --> 00:28:00,797
We're trying to find
a common denominator that explains

246
00:28:00,922 --> 00:28:03,214
why the players were chosen.

247
00:28:03,672 --> 00:28:05,422
Any ideas?

248
00:28:07,297 --> 00:28:11,005
First, let's decide
what to do about the vote.

249
00:28:13,630 --> 00:28:20,255
I propose that we join forces to eliminate
players who pose a threat.

250
00:28:20,380 --> 00:28:24,464
We're going to save the hostages.
We can't let anyone else die.

251
00:28:24,589 --> 00:28:28,714
All we can do
is try to keep casualties to a minimum.

252
00:28:29,339 --> 00:28:33,339
You're proposing
that the three of us kill someone?

253
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:35,547
Yes, I am.

254
00:28:36,797 --> 00:28:39,589
-If I could, I'd have...
-Kiju!

255
00:28:45,089 --> 00:28:46,505
Who would we choose?

256
00:28:51,089 --> 00:28:53,172
Who is the most dangerous?

257
00:28:53,714 --> 00:28:58,172
The flight attendant in Singapore
doesn't pose a threat.

258
00:28:58,547 --> 00:29:02,672
That leaves one.
Kuranosuke Higa in Naha.

259
00:29:03,130 --> 00:29:07,596
He's dangerous.
His success came from betraying others.

260
00:29:07,755 --> 00:29:14,255
See how hated he is.
He'd sacrifice you in a heartbeat.

261
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:20,214
If someone deleted Christina's video,
it must have been him.

262
00:29:20,630 --> 00:29:24,297
Then we vote him out. Agreed?

263
00:29:24,422 --> 00:29:27,672
Wait! His mother is being held hostage.

264
00:29:27,797 --> 00:29:31,547
She has cancer.
She wouldn't live long anyway.

265
00:29:33,005 --> 00:29:39,214
The lives of your daughter and my sister
are far more valuable.

266
00:29:41,297 --> 00:29:43,255
Well, that settles it.

267
00:29:45,028 --> 00:29:47,649
I'll see you at the vote count.

268
00:29:53,047 --> 00:29:54,672
You're okay with this?

269
00:29:58,547 --> 00:29:59,672
One more thing.

270
00:30:01,464 --> 00:30:05,964
As a fellow collaborator,
I'd like to know your missions.

271
00:30:07,013 --> 00:30:08,180
What's yours?

272
00:30:08,591 --> 00:30:12,299
Oh, it's work-related. Like yours, probably.

273
00:30:15,964 --> 00:30:19,339
I'll tell you when the time comes.

274
00:30:20,297 --> 00:30:21,630
Likewise.

275
00:30:49,576 --> 00:30:53,005
Nobody stands in my way.

276
00:31:01,409 --> 00:31:04,382
To win a case, forget ideology, principles,

277
00:31:04,716 --> 00:31:07,174
and moral and ethical sensibilities.

278
00:31:07,323 --> 00:31:10,665
What about good and evil?
Isn't our job to...

279
00:31:10,790 --> 00:31:13,124
True good and evil don't exist.

280
00:31:15,790 --> 00:31:18,999
Only information and analysis win cases.

281
00:31:26,785 --> 00:31:27,683
Sylvia...

282
00:31:28,624 --> 00:31:31,716
I want you to succeed in life, like me.

283
00:31:32,956 --> 00:31:34,956
Our parents would have felt the same.

284
00:31:36,063 --> 00:31:39,263
I know... Thank you.

285
00:31:53,165 --> 00:31:55,290
That lawyer might be right.

286
00:31:56,020 --> 00:31:57,343
You're voting for Higa?

287
00:31:57,377 --> 00:31:59,877
If not, you might be eliminated.

288
00:32:00,750 --> 00:32:02,582
What about saving everyone?

289
00:32:04,999 --> 00:32:09,082
You just want to win, don't you?

290
00:32:10,040 --> 00:32:12,540
Is this the "right thing"?

291
00:32:15,165 --> 00:32:18,915
It seems it was a mistake
to team up with you.

292
00:32:20,665 --> 00:32:23,332
I won't let them kill Higa's mother!

293
00:32:26,874 --> 00:32:28,124
Kiju!

294
00:32:35,457 --> 00:32:39,582
ELIMINATION GAME
4 HOURS UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

295
00:32:59,457 --> 00:33:03,540
I NEED TO DISCUSS SOMETHING WITH YOU.
PLEASE CALL ME. HAN KIJU

296
00:33:11,082 --> 00:33:12,176
Is that you, Higa?

297
00:33:15,186 --> 00:33:15,696
Yes.

298
00:33:16,769 --> 00:33:20,790
The lawyer, Andy...
He plans to vote you out.

299
00:33:21,207 --> 00:33:24,665
He approached me and Niide about it.

300
00:33:24,915 --> 00:33:27,915
But I refused.

301
00:33:29,624 --> 00:33:35,463
I can't help you, but I wanted you to know.

302
00:33:36,430 --> 00:33:40,410
Got it. Thanks.

303
00:33:49,707 --> 00:33:54,332
Also, I heard about your mother.

304
00:33:57,707 --> 00:34:04,082
If I'm alive when this game's over,

305
00:34:05,832 --> 00:34:07,832
let me examine her.

306
00:34:10,275 --> 00:34:10,996
Bye.

307
00:34:12,138 --> 00:34:13,221
Wait!

308
00:34:17,143 --> 00:34:18,957
He's targeting you, not me.

309
00:34:22,161 --> 00:34:25,995
Before you wrote to me,
I got a message from Andy.

310
00:34:26,447 --> 00:34:29,656
"I have discovered what Kiju's mission is.

311
00:34:29,781 --> 00:34:32,072
"He could easily complete it.

312
00:34:32,447 --> 00:34:37,322
"Let's work together.
He must be eliminated first."

313
00:34:39,572 --> 00:34:41,864
Your mission is to kill a patient?

314
00:34:43,197 --> 00:34:44,822
Commit murder.

315
00:34:45,031 --> 00:34:48,531
You could do it whenever you feel like it.

316
00:34:48,822 --> 00:34:53,197
Andy sent Singapore the same message.

317
00:34:53,447 --> 00:34:56,031
Wait, please!

318
00:34:56,281 --> 00:35:02,822
No! Please, my daughter... Rian...

319
00:35:03,364 --> 00:35:06,114
You have two votes even if I abstain.

320
00:35:09,447 --> 00:35:13,281
Could you vote for Andy?
I'll ask Niide,

321
00:35:13,406 --> 00:35:18,322
that'll make three.

322
00:35:18,447 --> 00:35:20,365
So you'll vote for the lawyer?

323
00:35:23,156 --> 00:35:25,225
You're fine killing Andy's sister?

324
00:35:26,697 --> 00:35:29,114
I thought you couldn't kill.

325
00:35:30,989 --> 00:35:33,281
Sorry, I'm not cooperating.

326
00:35:48,364 --> 00:35:52,406
ELIMINATION GAME

327
00:36:13,197 --> 00:36:15,281
NOTIFICATION

328
00:36:33,031 --> 00:36:34,864
I spoke to the police.

329
00:36:34,989 --> 00:36:37,906
No doubt you are in dire straits.

330
00:36:38,739 --> 00:36:40,989
I know you don't want to kill.

331
00:36:41,114 --> 00:36:47,114
But please remember
that Rian is everything to us.

332
00:36:47,364 --> 00:36:49,489
Her happiness is everything.

333
00:36:50,531 --> 00:36:52,364
She is all that matters.

334
00:36:52,531 --> 00:36:55,239
I can be the wife of a murderer.

335
00:36:56,114 --> 00:37:02,322
So save Rian, I beg you.

336
00:37:07,822 --> 00:37:12,156
All right... All right.

337
00:37:30,998 --> 00:37:33,748
WE NEED TO TALK.
MEET ME AT THE SHRINE.

338
00:37:54,857 --> 00:37:57,482
-Here he comes.
-Mr. Niide!

339
00:37:58,857 --> 00:38:03,149
Where are you going, Mr. Niide?
What's your mission?

340
00:38:03,274 --> 00:38:06,607
No comment. Let me through.

341
00:38:06,732 --> 00:38:09,691
-Please answer me.
-Leave, now!

342
00:38:12,732 --> 00:38:16,332
Mr. Niide, what's your sin?
What did you do?

343
00:38:16,423 --> 00:38:19,007
-Are you enjoying your fame?
-Move.

344
00:38:19,132 --> 00:38:21,623
Violence again? I'm a pacifist!

345
00:38:22,493 --> 00:38:28,368
Those are the eyes of a dangerous man!
"Wrath"! Eyes filled with rage!

346
00:38:31,660 --> 00:38:32,543
Leave.

347
00:38:39,990 --> 00:38:43,365
ELIMINATION GAME
1 HOUR UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

348
00:38:58,691 --> 00:38:59,857
What's this about?

349
00:39:00,607 --> 00:39:02,982
You're conspiring against me.

350
00:39:03,649 --> 00:39:05,691
You did well to find that out.

351
00:39:06,590 --> 00:39:08,340
It doesn't matter anymore.

352
00:39:11,774 --> 00:39:16,543
No. It's you who is eliminated.

353
00:39:22,603 --> 00:39:25,519
Threatening me won't change the vote, doctor.

354
00:39:25,978 --> 00:39:28,103
This is not about vote.

355
00:39:28,478 --> 00:39:30,223
This is about saving my daughter.

356
00:39:30,715 --> 00:39:32,257
So, are you going to kill me?

357
00:39:32,603 --> 00:39:34,603
Yeah. Why not?

358
00:39:35,103 --> 00:39:38,269
Interesting. Do it.

359
00:39:40,769 --> 00:39:43,394
Come on. Do it.

360
00:39:44,478 --> 00:39:45,394
Do it!

361
00:39:49,103 --> 00:39:53,394
You can't. You can't kill.
You just can't.

362
00:39:57,811 --> 00:40:00,769
It has been like that.
Until now!

363
00:40:01,269 --> 00:40:06,019
So are you ready to bring death to
my innocent sister, Mrs. Niide and others?

364
00:40:06,561 --> 00:40:10,686
That's right. Or only my daughter will die.

365
00:40:10,853 --> 00:40:14,103
And how will your daughter's future
look like if she lives?

366
00:40:15,478 --> 00:40:19,061
How much colder and darker will her future be

367
00:40:19,644 --> 00:40:21,811
when her father's in jail for murder?

368
00:40:21,978 --> 00:40:24,394
Do you honestly think you're capable of
giving her a worthwhile...

369
00:40:24,519 --> 00:40:25,769
Shut up!

370
00:40:31,478 --> 00:40:33,436
Rian has a dream.

371
00:40:35,186 --> 00:40:37,269
I don't care what happens to me.

372
00:40:39,269 --> 00:40:41,644
I'll save Rian, no matter what!

373
00:40:43,144 --> 00:40:44,894
Kiju, stop!

374
00:40:45,144 --> 00:40:47,478
-Let go!
-Don't do it!

375
00:40:54,311 --> 00:40:55,728
So they were your thugs.

376
00:40:56,103 --> 00:40:57,811
You're late, detective.

377
00:41:00,019 --> 00:41:03,228
Did you get the part
where Han Kiju tried to kill me?

378
00:41:03,519 --> 00:41:05,144
Yes, I did, sir.

379
00:41:05,353 --> 00:41:08,063
Send copies to Naha and Singapore at once.

380
00:41:08,678 --> 00:41:12,063
Now everyone is going to vote for you.

381
00:41:13,686 --> 00:41:17,394
-No! No! I have to kill him!
-Kiju!

382
00:41:17,561 --> 00:41:21,516
You see? I called you to come here
to see his true nature.

383
00:41:23,353 --> 00:41:26,686
I JUST RECEIVED A MESSAGE FROM A MAN
FROM SEOUL TO COME TO THE SHRINE.

384
00:41:27,728 --> 00:41:32,603
-Niide, please, let me go...
-Stop!

385
00:41:32,769 --> 00:41:36,728
If you don't want your wife to die,
you'd better watch him until the vote.

386
00:41:37,853 --> 00:41:42,561
-Come on! I'll kill you!
-Kiju!

387
00:42:18,311 --> 00:42:24,811
It's all your fault...
Why... Why?!

388
00:42:47,519 --> 00:42:51,894
It's hopeless...

389
00:43:10,171 --> 00:43:13,879
I'm sorry, Rian...

390
00:43:20,894 --> 00:43:22,603
Let me die!

391
00:43:23,686 --> 00:43:27,728
If I die, Rian will be saved!

392
00:43:27,978 --> 00:43:29,686
It's not over yet!

393
00:43:31,061 --> 00:43:35,149
I can't trust what you say anymore...
I don't believe you!

394
00:43:36,896 --> 00:43:39,061
You don't have to trust me.

395
00:43:39,186 --> 00:43:42,490
But do as I say.

396
00:43:43,119 --> 00:43:49,823
Vote to eliminate me.
Whatever you do, just vote for me.

397
00:44:27,437 --> 00:44:30,562
ELIMINATION GAME
1 MINUTE UNTIL THE VOTE COUNT

398
00:44:31,106 --> 00:44:33,606
PM 03:59 JST

399
00:45:02,985 --> 00:45:05,544
It's time. Cast your votes.

400
00:45:06,482 --> 00:45:09,818
The player with the most votes
will be eliminated.

401
00:45:48,819 --> 00:45:50,735
Let the tally begin.

402
00:46:28,152 --> 00:46:29,652
So much for teamwork.

403
00:46:38,110 --> 00:46:39,902
You double-crosser...

404
00:46:56,485 --> 00:46:59,069
Hey! Why me?!

405
00:47:05,610 --> 00:47:08,860
The player with the most votes
will be eliminated.

406
00:47:52,319 --> 00:47:55,027
This is your doing, isn't it? Toshiro Niide.

407
00:47:55,985 --> 00:47:57,277
What do you mean?

408
00:47:59,777 --> 00:48:03,089
Why did you lie to me?!
You said we'd all vote for the computer guy!

409
00:48:03,676 --> 00:48:10,944
Niide, I voted for Andy because I expected
you and Kiju to do the same.

410
00:48:11,235 --> 00:48:12,527
What's going on?

411
00:48:15,694 --> 00:48:18,363
We can't afford for
more players to be eliminated!

412
00:48:19,016 --> 00:48:22,325
More hostages will die!
This was the only solution.

413
00:48:26,226 --> 00:48:29,726
Andy, I knew from the start
that you'd make contact.

414
00:48:31,194 --> 00:48:34,110
And I knew from what you say,
that you'd vote for Kiju.

415
00:48:37,069 --> 00:48:41,110
Kiju didn't want to vote for anyone.
That's why I made him vote for me.

416
00:48:41,235 --> 00:48:43,152
And I voted for Janice.

417
00:48:43,444 --> 00:48:46,694
That gave the three of us one vote each.

418
00:48:47,652 --> 00:48:49,652
I asked Janice to vote for Higa.

419
00:48:49,944 --> 00:48:53,360
Janice, I have one request.

420
00:48:53,485 --> 00:48:56,652
Yes. And you tried to kick me out!

421
00:48:57,069 --> 00:49:00,152
If someone else voted for me, Tony would die!

422
00:49:00,777 --> 00:49:03,569
I tried to be kind because you helped me
and this is how you repay me?!

423
00:49:04,027 --> 00:49:05,944
I knew nobody would vote for you.

424
00:49:06,194 --> 00:49:09,902
But... but...

425
00:49:12,027 --> 00:49:14,569
How'd you know I'd vote for Andy.

426
00:49:14,694 --> 00:49:18,569
Kiju doesn't want your mother to die.
He was bound to contact you.

427
00:49:18,735 --> 00:49:22,402
Andy plots to sabotage others
while Kiju tries to save them.

428
00:49:22,527 --> 00:49:28,319
I asked myself, who would you trust?
Who would you keep around?

429
00:49:30,860 --> 00:49:34,527
You can't eliminate anyone... it's a tie.

430
00:49:35,735 --> 00:49:36,610
Indeed.

431
00:49:37,319 --> 00:49:38,485
We won.

432
00:49:40,152 --> 00:49:44,735
If you had lost, you would have been spared
the hell that's to come.

433
00:49:46,110 --> 00:49:51,196
You are rivals.
Mortal enemies in a fight to the death.

434
00:49:52,770 --> 00:49:57,110
Take a good, long look now.
Before you kill each other.

435
00:49:57,819 --> 00:50:03,944
Enjoy your prisoner's dilemma.
The elimination game has just begun!

436
00:50:09,235 --> 00:50:14,110
Niide... So you don't have the guts
to sacrifice someone.

437
00:50:15,360 --> 00:50:17,985
Andy, I need to ask you something!

438
00:50:18,319 --> 00:50:22,556
Did you represent a driver
who died in Tokyo five years ago?

439
00:50:25,756 --> 00:50:29,532
Answer me!
This could lead to the Mastermind.

440
00:50:29,557 --> 00:50:33,515
An event from five years ago
may connect us.

441
00:50:34,790 --> 00:50:36,290
I don't remember.

442
00:50:37,748 --> 00:50:42,123
What about you two?
Were you in Tokyo five years ago?

443
00:50:42,707 --> 00:50:43,790
No.

444
00:50:43,998 --> 00:50:44,729
Me neither.

445
00:50:45,915 --> 00:50:48,873
You're just trying to find the Mastermind
to complete your mission.

446
00:50:49,064 --> 00:50:53,481
No! Niide's trying to do what's right!

447
00:50:55,582 --> 00:50:59,665
He's doing it for us!
He's trying to rescue the hostages!

448
00:51:02,457 --> 00:51:06,910
Look, we got through this predicament
thanks to him.

449
00:51:08,373 --> 00:51:13,915
He's shown that if we work together,
we can beat that criminal!

450
00:51:14,123 --> 00:51:20,623
He's shown that we can save our loved ones!

451
00:51:24,998 --> 00:51:29,040
You're right... We won this time.

452
00:51:38,780 --> 00:51:40,323
I guess I should thank you.

453
00:51:43,270 --> 00:51:44,249
Thanks.

454
00:52:13,915 --> 00:52:15,540
This is a nice spot.

455
00:52:17,582 --> 00:52:18,790
Yeah.

456
00:52:20,957 --> 00:52:23,040
When did you think of it?

457
00:52:25,165 --> 00:52:27,123
Dunno...

458
00:52:30,087 --> 00:52:32,835
I was just looking for the "right thing."

459
00:52:40,887 --> 00:52:42,856
You had me fooled.

460
00:52:46,156 --> 00:52:47,582
Sorry.

461
00:52:50,123 --> 00:52:55,915
Andy might have been watching,
and you had lost your cool.

462
00:52:58,665 --> 00:53:00,040
I know...

463
00:53:00,873 --> 00:53:07,540
But no lies or secrets from now on.

464
00:53:16,429 --> 00:53:17,348
Sure.

465
00:53:20,157 --> 00:53:22,323
Let's get through this together.

466
00:53:23,196 --> 00:53:23,957
Yeah.

467
00:53:31,683 --> 00:53:32,516
Niide?

468
00:53:37,863 --> 00:53:43,582
I think our moves are being anticipated.

469
00:53:50,109 --> 00:53:51,415
By the mastermind?

470
00:53:52,957 --> 00:53:54,290
Yeah.

471
00:54:08,728 --> 00:54:13,082
It's like someone's predicting
and countering my every move.

472
00:54:14,123 --> 00:54:16,498
Even so, you won this time.

473
00:54:17,582 --> 00:54:19,165
This time, yeah...

474
00:54:31,373 --> 00:54:32,707
Don't move!

475
00:54:34,915 --> 00:54:38,040
Is this guy's life worth a lot?
